              "command": "grep -n \"load_forecast_frames\\|lead_time_delta\\|time_delta_input\\|def __getitem__\\|forecast\" /home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop/workshop_infrastructure/datasets/helio.py | head -60"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01E9KUWsGXhc8AYQ3aGsjNnq",
            "raw_output": "324:    forecast targets for temporal prediction tasks. Handles variable input\n339:        time_delta_input_minutes: List of candidate input time offsets in minutes, sorted ascending.\n343:        time_delta_target_minutes: Step size in minutes between forecast frames.\n345:            Only used when ``load_forecast_frames=True``.\n347:            \u2264 ``len(time_delta_input_minutes)``.\n348:        rollout_steps: Number of additional forecast steps beyond the first target frame.\n350:            Only used when ``load_forecast_frames=True``.\n389:        load_forecast_frames: If True (default), load both input and forecast frames and include\n390:            ``forecast`` and ``lead_time_delta`` in the returned sample. Set to False for downstream\n399:        time_delta_input_minutes: list[int],\n423:        load_forecast_frames: bool = True,\n448:        self.load_forecast_frames = load_forecast_frames\n478:        self.time_delta_input_minutes = sorted(\n479:            np.timedelta64(t, \"m\") for t in time_delta_input_minutes\n529:        When ``load_forecast_frames=False``, only input-frame offsets are checked, so the\n532:        if self.load_forecast_frames:\n534:            time_deltas = np.unique(self.time_delta_input_minutes + self.time_delta_target_minutes)\n536:            time_deltas = np.unique(self.time_delta_input_minutes)\n567:    def __getitem__(self, idx: int) -> dict:\n577:                time_delta_input (np.ndarray): (T,) \u2014 input time offsets in hours (relative to \"now\")\n578:            When ``load_forecast_frames=True`` (default), also includes:\n579:                forecast (np.ndarray):         (C, L, H, W) \u2014 target frames\n580:                lead_time_delta (np.ndarray):  (L,) \u2014 lead times in hours (negative = future)\n583:                forecast_latitude (list[float])  \u2014 only when ``load_forecast_frames=True``\n611:        Samples historical input frames randomly from ``time_delta_input_minutes``,\n617:        # The last entry in time_delta_input_minutes is always the \"now\" frame (offset 0\n622:            sorted(random.sample(self.time_delta_input_minutes[:-1], self.n_input_timestamps - 1))\n623:            + [self.time_delta_input_minutes[-1]]\n633:        time_delta_input_float = (\n639:            \"time_delta_input\": time_delta_input_float,\n642:        if self.load_forecast_frames:\n645:            sample[\"forecast\"] = self._load_and_stack_frames(target_timesteps)\n646:            sample[\"lead_time_delta\"] = (\n652:            if self.load_forecast_frames:\n653:                sample[\"forecast\"] = np.flip(sample[\"forecast\"], axis=-2).copy()\n659:            if self.load_forecast_frames:\n660:                sample[\"forecast_latitude\"] = [get_earth(ts).lat.value for ts in target_timesteps]",
