      "id": "1ed3c9e5-8f51-4a41-a613-60bf862dc38a",
      "type": "msg",
      "mentions": [],
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
    },
    {
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "body": "This error has nothing to do with your data pipeline \u2014 it's WandB trying to interactively prompt you to log in, and your Jupyter frontend doesn't support that.\n\nLook at the sequence right before the traceback:\n```\nwandb: ERROR Failed to detect the name of this notebook...\nwandb: (1) Create a W&B account\nwandb: (2) Use an existing W&B account\nwandb: (3) Don't visualize my results\n```\nthen immediately:\n```\nStdinNotImplementedError: raw_input was called, but this frontend does not support input requests.\n```\n\n`WandbLogger` doesn't actually connect to WandB when you construct it \u2014 it's lazy. The real connection (`wandb.init(...)`) only happens inside `trainer.fit()`, at `_call_setup_hook`, the first time Lightning touches `logger.experiment` (see the bottom of the traceback: `wandb.py:410 \u2192 wandb_init.py:1594 \u2192 wandb_login.py`). Since you haven't logged into WandB on this machine yet, it tries to fall back to an interactive prompt asking you to choose 1/2/3 \u2014 but this Jupyter setup can't send input back to a running cell (`_allow_stdin` is off), so it crashes instead of waiting for you to answer.\n\nThe markdown cell above (\"The first time you run WandB... a dialog box... paste your API key\") describes how this normally works in VS Code's Jupyter extension, which *does* support that stdin dialog \u2014 evidently this frontend doesn't.\n\nTwo ways to fix it:\n\n**Option A \u2014 log in once, outside the interactive prompt path.** Get your API key from https://wandb.ai/authorize, then either:\n- Run `wandb login <your-key>` in a terminal on this machine (stores it in `~/.netrc`), or\n- Add a cell before the trainer cell: `os.environ[\"WANDB_API_KEY\"] = \"<your-key>\"`\n\nEither way, `wandb.init()` will find the key non-interactively and skip the prompt entirely.\n\n**Option B \u2014 skip WandB for this test run.** Since you're just sanity-checking the baseline, drop `wandb_logger` from the trainer's `logger=[...]` list and keep just `csv_logger`. That avoids the login path altogether; you can add WandB back once you have a key set up.\n\nGiven you're just trying to confirm the baseline runs end-to-end, I'd go with Option B for now and set up WandB separately when you're ready to actually track runs. Want me to edit the trainer cell to drop `wandb_logger`?",
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1789504658.5953343,
      "raw_time": false,
      "mentions": [],
      "id": "f6a1462e-3113-436b-bc11-9661f2526681"
    },
    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789505478.0357385,
      "sender": "jpereira",
      "id": "c278dd81-a10f-4e37-b4d8-20476a34266d",
