        },
        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
        "settings": {}
      },
      "body": "how do i add the wandb login suggestion you made on the notebook? i tried it on the terminal and im confused (notebook) jovyan@jupyter-jpereira:~/tmp/surya_workshop$ wandb login jperei4@gmu.edu\nbash: wandb: command not found",
      "type": "msg"
    },
    {
      "time": 1789505486.6395838,
      "raw_time": false,
      "id": "d5f6a15e-5332-45f3-83a3-98707d5979e9",
      "mentions": [],
      "type": "msg",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "body": "Two separate issues there.\n\n**1. Wrong argument.** `wandb login` expects the **API key** (a long token from https://wandb.ai/authorize), not your email. The email is just how you sign into wandb.ai in the browser to *get* that key \u2014 it's not what you paste into the CLI.\n\n**2. `command not found`** \u2014 the `wandb` package is installed inside the `surya_ws` conda environment, but your terminal session hasn't activated it. The notebook kernel activates it for you automatically; a plain terminal shell does not.\n\nLet me check that's actually the case before you try again."
    },
