    {
      "body": "I don't have access to your API key \u2014 it's tied to your personal WandB account, so only you can retrieve it. Here's how:\n\n1. Go to **https://wandb.ai/authorize** in your browser.\n2. Log in with the account you were invited to the project with (the one tied to `jperei4@gmu.edu`, if that's the account \u2014 sign up first at wandb.ai if you haven't created one yet).\n3. That page shows a long alphanumeric string (~40 chars) \u2014 that's your API key. Copy it.\n4. You can also find it later anytime at **wandb.ai/settings** under \"API keys.\"\n\nThen use *that string* (not your email) as the argument:\n```bash\nwandb login <paste-the-long-key-here>\n```\n\nSince this key acts like a password for your account, don't paste it into files that get committed to git or share it anywhere public \u2014 just use it directly in the terminal command.",
      "raw_time": false,
