    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "Found it. `wandb` **is** installed (`/home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws/bin/wandb` exists) \u2014 the problem is `conda activate surya_ws` fails because that environment isn't registered under the name `surya_ws`; it was created at a custom path (`/home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws`) that conda doesn't recognize by name. You need to activate it **by full path** instead:\n\n```bash\nconda activate /home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws\n```\n\nThen:\n```bash\nwhich wandb\nwandb login <your-api-key>\n```\n\nThat should resolve it. Once `wandb login` succeeds, go back to the notebook and re-run the `trainer.fit(...)` cell \u2014 no other changes needed.",
