      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "That confirms it \u2014 same root cause as before, but this time it's baked into `FlareLightningModule` itself, not the notebook. The model summary table and the \"Sanity Checking\" progress bar you saw aren't a result \u2014 Lightning always runs a quick validation pass (the \"sanity check\") *before* training starts, and that's exactly where this crashed:\n\n```\nFile .../lightning_modules/pl_flare_baseline.py:239, in validation_step\n    target = batch[\"forecast\"].unsqueeze(1).float()\nKeyError: 'forecast'\n```\n\n`pl_flare_baseline.py` still hardcodes `batch[\"forecast\"]` as the label key \u2014 it wasn't updated when the dataset's label key got renamed to `ground_truth`. Let me check the rest of that file for other occurrences before fixing it."
    },
    {
      "id": "0a9adcf8-42d0-4e79-9028-e35c2edfa3c7",
