            },
            "title": "Read pl_flare_baseline.py (1 - 40)",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01UfXjHKZi4mM6gp2ZzwyxW9",
            "raw_output": "1\t\"\"\"\n2\tpl_simple_baseline.py\n3\t\n4\tA minimal PyTorch Lightning wrapper for training a flare prediction model.\n5\t\n6\tThis module defines a single LightningModule (FlareLightningModule) that:\n7\t  - Calls a user-provided PyTorch model on batched inputs (batch[\"ts\"])\n8\t  - Computes one or more training/validation losses via a user-provided loss function\n9\t  - Logs scalar losses and evaluation metrics using Lightning's built-in logging\n10\t  - Configures a simple Adam optimizer\n11\t\n12\tIntended use:\n13\t  - Provide a clean, readable baseline training loop in Lightning\n14\t  - Separate \"model architecture\" from \"training mechanics\"\n15\t  - Demonstrate how to log multiple losses/metrics consistently\n16\t\n17\tKey batch contract:\n18\t  - batch[\"ts\"]       : torch.Tensor input stack (e.g., [B, C, T, H, W])\n19\t  - batch[\"forecast\"] : torch.Tensor target values (e.g., [B] or [B,])\n20\t\n21\tOptional preprocessing:\n22\t  - If ``preprocess_fn`` is provided to ``__init__``, it is called on the batch dict\n23\t    before every model call. This is the intended hook for input transformations (such\n24\t    as inverse-normalizing SDO channels) that should not live inside the model.\n25\t\n26\tKey metrics contract (the `metrics` dict passed to __init__):\n27\t  - metrics[\"train_loss\"]    : callable(output, target) -> (loss_dict, weight_list)\n28\t        Backpropagated. Logged as \"train_loss\".\n29\t  - metrics[\"val_loss\"]      : callable(output, target) -> (loss_dict, weight_list)\n30\t        Optional. Logged as \"val_loss\" and therefore what ModelCheckpoint monitors.\n31\t        Falls back to metrics[\"train_loss\"] when absent.\n32\t  - metrics[\"train_metrics\"] : callable(output, target) -> (metric_dict, weight_list)\n33\t  - metrics[\"val_metrics\"]   : callable(output, target) -> (metric_dict, weight_list)\n34\t        Reported only. These do NOT affect checkpoint selection \u2014 \"val_loss\" does.\n35\t\n36\tWhere:\n37\t  - loss_dict / metric_dict map string names -> torch scalar tensors\n38\t  - weight_list is a list-like of floats (or tensors) aligned with the dict iteration order\n39\t    used by this baseline to form a weighted sum loss.\n40\t\"\"\""
          },
